        ("BEGINNER", "Which of the following is true about a derived class?", ["It inherits members from its base class and may add new ones", "It cannot have its own member functions", "It is always abstract", "It shares the same object layout as the base"], "A", "A derived class inherits base members and can extend them with additional members."),
        ("BEGINNER", "What happens when you call a non-virtual member function through a base pointer?", ["It calls the derived override", "It calls the base version regardless of the dynamic type", "It causes a compile error", "It calls both versions"], "B", "Without virtual dispatch the compiler selects the base version based on the static type of the pointer."),
