        ("INTERMEDIATE", "class A { public: void f() { std::cout << 'A'; } }; class B : public A { public: void f() { std::cout << 'B'; } }; B b; b.f(); What is printed?", ["A", "AB", "B", "BA"], "C", "B::f hides A::f, and since b is a B the call resolves to B::f, printing B."),
        ("INTERMEDIATE", "class A { public: virtual void f() { std::cout << 'A'; } }; class B : public A { public: void f() { std::cout << 'B'; } }; A *p = new B; p->f(); What is printed?", ["A", "AB", "Compile error", "B"], "D", "virtual enables dynamic dispatch, so p->f() calls B::f based on the object's dynamic type, printing B."),
        ("INTERMEDIATE", "class Animal { public: virtual void speak() { std::cout << 'A'; } }; class Dog : public Animal { public: void speak() { std::cout << 'W'; } }; Animal *a = new Dog; a->speak(); What is printed?", ["A", "W", "AW", "Nothing"], "B", "Dynamic dispatch routes the virtual call to Dog::speak, which prints W."),
        ("INTERMEDIATE", "What does a protected member of a base class become in a derived class under public inheritance?", ["Protected", "Public", "Private", "Inaccessible"], "A", "Under public inheritance, protected base members remain protected in the derived class."),
        ("INTERMEDIATE", "class Base { public: virtual void f() = 0; }; Why can Base not be instantiated?", ["It has no destructor", "It contains a pure virtual function", "It is declared with the keyword abstract", "It has no data members"], "B", "A class with at least one pure virtual function is abstract, so instantiating it is a compile error."),
        ("INTERMEDIATE", "class D : public B { }; Which part of the base is NOT accessible to code inside D?", ["Public member functions", "Protected data", "Private data", "Public data"], "C", "Private members are not inherited or visible to derived classes; only public and protected members are accessible."),
        ("INTERMEDIATE", "class Shape { public: virtual double area() const = 0; }; class Square : public Shape { public: double side; double area() const { return side * side; } }; Square s; s.side = 4; Shape *p = &s; std::cout << p->area(); What is printed?", ["16", "8", "4", "0"], "A", "p points to a Square and the virtual call dispatches to Square::area, computing 4 * 4 = 16."),
